# The build context is the repository root, and the image carries three things
# out of it: the loader's sources (loader/), the front door's configuration
# (docker/instance/) and the seed bundle scripts/build-image.sh writes to
# .docker-context/ before the build. Everything else is kept out, so the
# context stays small and a file that changes cannot change the image.
#
# The instance's own code does not come through the context at all: it reaches
# the image as the history inside the seed bundle.
*
!docker
docker/*
!docker/instance
!docker/instance/**
!loader
!loader/**
!.docker-context
!.docker-context/**
